            "algebra"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "step-2-1",
          "claim": "The difference $\\bar x-\\mu_0=(-1,-1)^T$ has squared Euclidean norm $2$. Therefore [F2] gives $T^2=4(3/2)\\cdot2=12$, and the scale $(n-p)/(p(n-1))=2/(2\\cdot3)=1/3$ makes the F statistic equal $4$.",
          "step": "2.1",
          "inputs": [
